+displacer_seq is the seq of the displacer's ACCEPTED event, or of its
+  REJECTED event: add_path() can remove old paths and then meet one that
+  dominates the new path (fuzzy dominance is not transitive); null if that
+  event was not recorded (event cap)
+dominator_path_id, other_pathtype on REJECTED events: the path in the rel's
+  pathlist that dominated this one, and its type.  Present only with
+  coverage.add_path_rejected_dominator; null if the id could not be assigned
+  (event cap).  There is no dominator_seq: the dominator was accepted
+  earlier, possibly without a recorded event; find it by path_id
+gap_cost of a REJECTED event is cost_total minus the dominator's total;
+  negative when the path lost on startup cost, pathkeys or
+  parameterization rather than on total
 ```
 
